      "description": "Mean packet loss at 1400B across the watchdog's two probe targets. THIS is what the auto-bounce decides on: it fires when the mean is >=10% on 3 of the last 5 probes (60s cadence). Small-packet loss reads far lower and is why this fault stayed invisible for months \u2014 56B read 0.0% while 1400B read 24.4% on the same path. Per-target series are shown for corroboration; a single target over threshold does NOT trigger.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "dashed"
            }
          },
          "decimals": 1,
          "thresholds": {
